From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Subject: [PATCH] t20: accept the vendor frame-channel ioctl ABI

OpenIMP (and the stock T20 libimp) do not use the generic V4L2 S_FMT
number on the frame channel.  They send the vendor ioctls, notably
0xc07056c3 (SET_FMT with the 0x70-byte t20 format), 0x407056c4
(GET_FMT) and 0x80045612/0x80045613 (STREAM_ON/OFF).  The scaler,
bank/depth and listen-buffer numbers already match
VIDIOC_DEFAULT_CMD_{SET_SCALER,SET_BANKS,LISTEN_BUF}.

frame_channel_vidioc_default() returned -ISP_ERROR for SET_FMT, so
OpenIMP's IMP_FrameSource_EnableChn() failed at "set format failed"
before any buffer was queued.

Translate the vendor numbers into the existing generic handlers.  The
0x70-byte format begins with a normal struct v4l2_format; the T20 crop
and scaler fields are programmed by the separate ioctls.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
---
--- a/driver/t20/sdk/source/tx-isp-frame-channel.c
+++ b/driver/t20/sdk/source/tx-isp-frame-channel.c
@@ -827,6 +827,40 @@
 			ret = v4l2_subdev_call(vdev->parent, core, ioctl,
 					       cmd, arg);
 			break;
+		/*
+		 * T20 vendor frame-channel ABI used by OpenIMP/libimp.  The
+		 * stock T20 driver exposes these ioctl numbers instead of the
+		 * generic V4L2 ones; the 0x70-byte format starts with a normal
+		 * struct v4l2_format, followed by T20 crop/scaler fields that
+		 * are programmed through the separate ioctls below.
+		 */
+		case 0xc07056c3: { /* T20 VIDIOC_SET_FMT */
+			struct v4l2_format vf;
+
+			memset(&vf, 0, sizeof(vf));
+			memcpy(&vf, arg, sizeof(vf));
+			ret = frame_channel_vidioc_s_fmt_vid_cap(file, fh,
+								 &vf);
+			memcpy(arg, &vf, sizeof(vf));
+			break;
+		}
+		case 0x407056c4: { /* T20 VIDIOC_GET_FMT */
+			struct v4l2_format vf;
+
+			memset(&vf, 0, sizeof(vf));
+			ret = frame_channel_vidioc_g_fmt_vid_cap(file, fh,
+								 &vf);
+			memcpy(arg, &vf, sizeof(vf));
+			break;
+		}
+		case 0x80045612: /* T20 VIDIOC_STREAM_ON */
+			ret = frame_channel_vidioc_streamon(file, fh,
+					V4L2_BUF_TYPE_VIDEO_CAPTURE);
+			break;
+		case 0x80045613: /* T20 VIDIOC_STREAM_OFF */
+			ret = frame_channel_vidioc_streamoff(file, fh,
+					V4L2_BUF_TYPE_VIDEO_CAPTURE);
+			break;
 		default:
 			ret = -ISP_ERROR;
 			break;
